    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP leans into high-upside favorable matchups today, with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge at a commanding 82.37. Facing Elder, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a stellar platoon alignment and a prime #2 spot in the lineup, making him the undisputed anchor of our outfield production. We are equally bullish on the trio of **Tyler Soderstrom** (74.23), **Max Muncy** (68.95), and **Henry Bolte** (65.40), who all draw favorable matchups against Bradford. The park factors in their venue provide a significant 10% boost, and Bradford\u2019s inflated 5.29 xERA suggests high run-scoring potential for this group. Despite the risk of \"Lineup Pending\" designations, the statistical path for **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Henry Bolte** remains the highest-ceiling play on the board.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Travis Bazzana**, who fell just shy of the starting cut with a 42.70 score. While **Travis Bazzana** carries value, his matchup against Mize\u2014paired with a suboptimal #7 batting order\u2014kept him behind the more efficient production expected from **Max Muncy**. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with **Brice Turang** (46.98); while he is our primary weapon for stolen bases, facing an elite arm like Skubal (2.77 xERA) significantly tempers his floor. We are opting to start him primarily for his speed-based utility, banking on his 85% stolen base success rate to manufacture value even against a tough lefty. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** on the IL and hope for his return, as his absence currently leaves a void in our core production that forces us to lean on high-variance plays like **Cole Young** and **Austin Riley**. Keep a close eye on the weather and confirmed lineups, as any late-breaking shifts in the order could necessitate a quick pivot for our bench options.",
